    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is minimal, coherent, and lands in exactly the right unit. `BusinessDays` already describes itself as the single source of truth for the effective registration date, so extending its private `rollToBusinessDay` to also skip holidays keeps the rule in one place \u2014 every caller (stored value, daily limit, bulk-signup warning) picks up the holiday behavior for free, with no duplication anywhere else.\n\nSpecifics that make it idiomatic here:\n- `HOLIDAYS` is a `private static final Set<LocalDate>` constant \u2014 the natural shape for a fixed lookup set, and `Set.contains` in the loop condition reads cleanly.\n- The existing one-day-at-a-time `while` loop was reused rather than reworked, so consecutive weekend/holiday runs (e.g. a holiday adjacent to a weekend) roll through correctly without any new branching logic.\n- The class and method Javadoc were both updated to match the new behavior, keeping the \"single source of truth\" documentation honest.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and no logic leaked into callers. A maintainer of this codebase would find this a natural edit.",
